WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.510
The Roman writer Suetonius recorded how
Julius Caesar wrote his secret letters.

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.450
For A, Caesar wrote the fourth letter, D.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.650
And so on through the alphabet.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.910
Every letter slides along by
the same amount: 3 places.

5
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.290
Now here's a message hidden the same way,

6
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.282
but nobody tells you the shift.

7
00:00:20.332 --> 00:00:23.210
YHQL.

8
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.310
If you intercepted this,
could you crack it?

9
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.290
In this mission, you'll see how a Caesar
cipher turns plaintext into ciphertext,

10
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.670
and why the shift is the key.

11
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.410
Then you'll meet three more
ciphers: one using a keyword,

12
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.070
one that zigzags letters across
rails, and one made of symbols.

13
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.920
Your mission: decide whether
you could crack Caesar's cipher.
